        "step_title": "SynoCli WiFi Tools",
        "items": [
            {
                "desc": "The tools to connect the NAS to a WiFi network, with the adapters of <b>synokernel-wifi</b>: load the driver of the adapter with <b>synocli-kernelmodule</b>, then connect with <b>synocli-wifi</b> and the profile of the network:<br><br><code>synocli-kernelmodule list</code><br><code>sudo -i synocli-kernelmodule --profile rtl88x2bu start</code><br><code>sudo -i synocli-wifi --profile MyNetwork start</code><br><br>To write the profile of a WiFi network:<br><code>sudo -i synocli-wifi new</code><br><br>Other options:<br><br>List the profiles:<br><code>sudo -i synocli-wifi list</code><br><br>Show the state of the connection:<br><code>sudo -i synocli-wifi status</code><br><br>Disconnect:<br><code>sudo -i synocli-wifi stop</code><br><br>See the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synocli-wifi-tools/\">package documentation</a>."
            }
        ]
